Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns & how we will use them  

• `user` (STRING, in the three photos tables) : unique uploader – we will count rows per `user`; each photo row is treated as one *click*.  
• `id` (STRING, in the three photos tables) : primary‑key of each photo, useful when we need to be sure every row is unique; can also be counted.  
• (no additional columns are strictly needed, but we may occasionally show `uploaded_date`, `storage_uri`, etc. just for sanity‑checks).

Typical filter: none – we simply need every photo from every versioned table.

────────────────────────────────────────────
Below are 10 progressively richer BigQuery SQL statements (all limited to 20 rows except the final answer).  
Replace nothing: table identifiers and column names are already properly quoted.

```sql
-- 1) Peek at a few user‑ids in the oldest collection
SELECT user
FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_1`
WHERE user IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) How many photos each user contributed in v_0_1
SELECT user, COUNT(*) AS photo_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_1`
GROUP BY user
ORDER BY photo_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Same idea for v_0_2
SELECT user, COUNT(*) AS photo_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_2`
GROUP BY user
ORDER BY photo_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Same idea for v_0_3
SELECT user, COUNT(*) AS photo_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_3`
GROUP BY user
ORDER BY photo_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Look at a combined stream of all user‑ids (first 20 rows only)
SELECT user
FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_1`
UNION ALL
SELECT user
FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_2`
UNION ALL
SELECT user
FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_3`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Global ranking of users by total clicks (photos) across every collection
SELECT user, COUNT(*) AS total_clicks
FROM (
  SELECT user
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_1`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT user
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_2`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT user
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_3`
)
GROUP BY user
ORDER BY total_clicks DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Same as #6 but with a CTE for readability
WITH all_photos AS (
  SELECT user FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_1`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT user FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_2`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT user FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_3`
)
SELECT user, COUNT(*) AS total_clicks
FROM all_photos
GROUP BY user
ORDER BY total_clicks DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Identify the single top user via a window function
WITH all_photos AS (
  SELECT user FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_1`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT user FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_2`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT user FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_3`
),
cnt AS (
  SELECT user, COUNT(*) AS total_clicks
  FROM all_photos
  GROUP BY user
)
SELECT user, total_clicks
FROM (
  SELECT user, total_clicks,
         RANK() OVER (ORDER BY total_clicks DESC) AS rnk
  FROM cnt
)
WHERE rnk = 1;
```

```sql
-- 9) Same but picking ties (dense_rank) if any
WITH all_photos AS (
  SELECT user FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_1`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT user FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_2`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT user FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_3`
)
SELECT user, COUNT(*) AS total_clicks
FROM all_photos
GROUP BY user
QUALIFY DENSE_RANK() OVER (ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC) = 1;
```

```sql
-- 10) Final concise answer: user(s) with the highest total clicks
SELECT user, COUNT(*) AS total_clicks
FROM (
  SELECT user FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_1`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT user FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_2`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT user FROM `bigquery-public-data.eclipse_megamovie.photos_v_0_3`
)
GROUP BY user
ORDER BY total_clicks DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

